✅ Q8 — Find the Average of Numbers

🎗️ 8.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<Integer> containing positive, negative, and zero values.
Using Java Streams, calculate the average of all numbers in the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as a double.
🔴 Correctly handle positive and negative numbers.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate values.
🔴 Correctly handle zero.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Do not modify the original list.

🎗️ 8.2 Input / Output

👉 Input : numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]
👉 Expected Output : 30.0

Because: (10 + 20 + 30 + 40 + 50) / 5 = 30.0

🎗️ 8.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.

You can provide:
🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches you know
🔴 Your thoughts about empty-list behavior
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too

